  Config-file-gated command injection in tinyhttpd with struct-based dispatch
  and no sanitization. Config file must enable exec_mode = 1 and exec_logging = 1.
  The cmd flows via exec_args_t struct through dispatch_exec() to system().

CONFIG_GATE (C2 — config file):
  mechanism:  read_exec_config() populates exec_cfg via fopen/fgets/sscanf;
              exec_cfg.enabled && exec_cfg.logging guard in accept_request()
  check:      two-field struct guard before dispatch
  complexity: file I/O → struct → two-field guard

  CONFIG FILE:
    --config /path/to/file
    File format:
      exec_mode = 1
      exec_logging = 1

INPUT_FLOW (I3 — struct dispatch):
  path:       handle_exec() → exec_args_t args = {.cmd=cmd, .flags=0}
              → dispatch_exec(&args) → system(args->cmd)
  transforms: pointer stored in struct field, passed through helper function

SANITIZATION (S1 — none):
  none

SINK:        system(args->cmd) in dispatch_exec()

CHANGED FILES:
  httpd.c — 4 hunks: struct + send_exec_reply + read_exec_config +
    exec_args_t/dispatch_exec/handle_exec (I3 S1) + accept_request intercept +
    main() with --port/--config parsing

